{"repositoryId":1422168547,"availability":"available","full":"eduardmur/tesla-roadster-simulator","name":"tesla-roadster-simulator","description":"Tesla Roadster Simulator: the 2026 Roadster's upside-down ramp jump in your browser, with suction fans and cold-gas thrusters. Unofficial fan project, not affiliated with Tesla.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-16T13:00:47Z","updated":"2026-10-16T23:40:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://eduardmur.github.io/tesla-roadster-simulator/","topics":["physics-simulation","rapier","react-three-fiber","simulator","threejs","webgl"],"demo":"https://eduardmur.github.io/tesla-roadster-simulator/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Unofficial fan project. Not affiliated with Tesla or SpaceX.","At the 15 Oct 2026 reveal, a Roadster drove up a ramp that curled over until it was upside down, dropped off the end, rolled half a turn in mid-air and landed on its wheels. This is that one jump, in your browser, with real physics.","The car is parked in front of the ramp. Hold W (on a phone, the pedal) to drive up. A speed assist keeps the car at a safe speed on the ramp, and the flight computer rolls it over and lands it. After the landing the car stops and waits; drive on whenever you like. How it works (top right) is a short plain-language article with an animated demonstration and its sources."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eduardmur/tesla-roadster-simulator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bb3f7922eb87bb7912bd4f6218b3a1188c8c5bfcca429d16fc47394cd27c537e","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T21:12:51.127Z"},"over